---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Q1 = `x ← 7

IF(x > 10)
{
  DISPLAY("big")
}
ELSE
{
  IF(x > 5)
  {
    DISPLAY("medium")
  }
  ELSE
  {
    DISPLAY("small")
  }
}`;
const Q4 = `let n = 12;

if (n > 5)
{
  console.log("A");
}
if (n > 10)
{
  console.log("B");
}`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Question Set 3</h1>

        <h4 class="text-sn-theme">
          Six questions &middot; 11 minutes &middot; cumulative
        </h4>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="objective">
          <h2>What This Is</h2>

          <p>Five exam-style questions covering Activity 1.1 through 1.15, weighted toward <b>chained and compound conditions</b>. Two are cumulative.</p>

          <p>
            <b>Set a timer for 11 minutes.</b> Work them out on paper; do not run
            the code. Mark each answer <b>sure</b> or <b>unsure</b>. Guess
            rather than leave a blank &mdash; the AP exam has no penalty for a
            wrong answer.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="questions">
          <h2>The Questions</h2>

          <p>
            Four have exactly one correct answer, one asks you to select{" "}
            <i>all</i> that apply, and the last is about data or the impact of
            computing rather than about code. <b>Thirteen of the exam's seventy
            questions look like that last one</b>, so it is on every set from
            here on.
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 1</h3>

          <p>What does this display?</p>

          <Code
            code={Q1}
            frame="code"
            lang="txt"
            title="Question 1 — exam notation"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mb-3"
          />

          <ul>
            <li>(A) <code>big</code></li>
            <li>(B) <code>medium</code></li>
            <li>(C) <code>small</code></li>
            <li>(D) <code>medium small</code></li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 2</h3>

          <p>A student wants to write the code above using <code>ELSE IF</code> in exam notation. What is the problem?</p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) Nothing. <code>ELSE IF</code> is valid exam notation.</li>
            <li>(B) <code>ELSE IF</code> exists but must be capitalized differently.</li>
            <li>(C) There is no <code>ELSE IF</code> on the reference sheet; chains are written as a nested <code>IF</code> inside an <code>ELSE</code>.</li>
            <li>(D) <code>ELSE IF</code> only works with numbers, not strings.</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 3 &mdash; Select all that apply</h3>

          <p>Given <code>a = true</code> and <code>b = false</code>, which expressions evaluate to <code>true</code>?</p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) <code>a &amp;&amp; b</code></li>
            <li>(B) <code>a || b</code></li>
            <li>(C) <code>!b</code></li>
            <li>(D) <code>!a &amp;&amp; !b</code></li>
            <li>(E) <code>a &amp;&amp; !b</code></li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 4</h3>

          <p>What does this code display?</p>

          <Code
            code={Q4}
            frame="code"
            lang="javascript"
            title="Question 4"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mb-3"
          />

          <ul>
            <li>(A) <code>A</code></li>
            <li>(B) <code>B</code></li>
            <li>(C) <code>A</code> then <code>B</code></li>
            <li>(D) Nothing</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 5</h3>

          <p>A program should charge a fee only when a customer is <b>not</b> a member <b>and</b> the order is under $25. Which condition is correct?</p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) <code>!isMember || total &lt; 25</code></li>
            <li>(B) <code>!isMember &amp;&amp; total &lt; 25</code></li>
            <li>(C) <code>isMember &amp;&amp; total &lt; 25</code></li>
            <li>(D) <code>!(isMember &amp;&amp; total &lt; 25)</code></li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 6 &mdash; Data and Impact</h3>

          <p>A photo taken on a phone stores the date, the camera model, and often the location. This information is called:</p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) Compression</li>
            <li>(B) A protocol</li>
            <li>(C) Binary</li>
            <li>(D) Metadata</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>
            Six answers, each marked <b>sure</b> or <b>unsure</b>, plus how far
            you got when the timer went off. Worth <b>2 points</b>, graded on
            completion.
          </p>
        </section>

        <h1
          class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
        >
          Start the Timer
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
